      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Perimeter of $AOC=2r+r\\theta$. — B1.\nAngle $COB=\\pi-\\theta$. — B1. Guidance: may be shown on the diagram; condone $180-\\theta$.\nPerimeter of $BOC=2r+r(\\pi-\\theta)$. — B1. Guidance: follow through on angle $COB$ if of the form $(k\\pi-\\theta)$, $k>0$.\n$2r+\\pi r-r\\theta=2(2r+r\\theta)$, giving $2+\\pi-\\theta=4+2\\theta$ and $\\theta=(\\pi-2)/3$. — M1. Guidance: set up the equation using $r(k\\pi-\\theta)$ and multiply the correct side by 2; condone omissions of $OA$, $OB$ and/or $OC$.\n$\\theta=0.38$. — A1. Guidance: equivalent answer in degrees scores A0.\nTotal: 5",
